        "original_id": "f9827de8-6bd9-56a0-99c6-b2b979d90556",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Proud To Commit Commercial Suicide\n- People: Jim Jones\n- Organizations: Nailbomb, Peoples Temple\n- Events: 1995 Dynamo Open Air Festival, Jonestown aftermath\n- Places: Jonestown, northwestern Guyana\n- Topics: live albums, industrial metal\n\nFacts:\n- Proud To Commit Commercial Suicide is a live Spanish-language album by the industrial metal band Nailbomb.\n- Proud To Commit Commercial Suicide captures Nailbomb's only live appearance at the 1995 Dynamo Open Air Festival.\n- The cover of Proud To Commit Commercial Suicide shows the aftermath of Jonestown.\n- Jonestown was a remote settlement in northwestern Guyana established by the Peoples Temple.\n- The Peoples Temple was an American socialist organization led by Jim Jones.",
